:PNLGRP.
:COPYR.(C) Copyright Quartz Systems 2026.
:HELP NAME=ADDAUTLE.Add Auth List Entry (ADDAUTLE)
:P.Use the Add Auth List Entry (ADDAUTLE) command to add users to an
authorization list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDAUTLE/AUTL'.Authorization list (AUTL)
:P.The authorization list that secures the object.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDAUTLE/USER'.Users (USER)
:P.The users for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:P.Up to 50 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*PUBLIC:EPK.
:PD.The public&colon. every user with no other authority.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDAUTLE/AUT'.Authority (AUT)
:P.The authority the public (users with no private authority and no
group authority) gets to the new object.
:P.Up to 11 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*USE:EPK.
:PD.Use authority&colon. the object can be read and run but not changed.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All authority&colon. the user can do anything with the object except
change its owner or what secures it.
:PT.:PK.*CHANGE:EPK.
:PD.Change authority&colon. all data authorities and operational
authority. The object can be used and its contents changed.
:PT.:PK.*EXCLUDE:EPK.
:PD.No authority&colon. the object cannot be used.
:PT.:PK.*OBJALTER:EPK.
:PD.Object alter authority.
:PT.:PK.*OBJEXIST:EPK.
:PD.Object existence authority.
:PT.:PK.*OBJMGT:EPK.
:PD.Object management authority.
:PT.:PK.*OBJOPR:EPK.
:PD.Object operational authority.
:PT.:PK.*OBJREF:EPK.
:PD.Object reference authority.
:PT.:PK.*ADD:EPK.
:PD.The new entries are added to what is there.
:PT.:PK.*DLT:EPK.
:PD.Delete authority.
:PT.:PK.*EXECUTE:EPK.
:PD.Execute authority.
:PT.:PK.*READ:EPK.
:PD.Read authority.
:PT.:PK.*UPD:EPK.
:PD.Update authority.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *AUTLMGT.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=ANZDFTPWD.Analyze Default Passwords (ANZDFTPWD)
:P.Use the Analyze Default Passwords (ANZDFTPWD) command to report the
profiles whose password is the profile name, and disable or expire them
when asked.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ANZDFTPWD/ACTION'.Action taken (ACTION)
:P.The action taken for this command.
:P.Up to 2 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *DISABLE, *PWDEXP.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=ANZPRFACT.Analyze Profile Activity (ANZPRFACT)
:P.Use the Analyze Profile Activity (ANZPRFACT) command to schedule the
job that disables profiles unused for the number of days given.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ANZPRFACT/DAYS'.Days of inactivity (DAYS)
:P.The days of inactivity for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*NOMAX:EPK.
:PD.No limit.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 3 digits. The value must be from 30 to 366.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CHGAUT.Change Authority (CHGAUT)
:P.Use the Change Authority (CHGAUT) command to change users' authority
to an IFS object.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGAUT/OBJ'.Object (OBJ)
:P.The object or objects the command works on, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGAUT/USER'.User (USER)
:P.The user for this command.
:P.Up to 50 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*PUBLIC:EPK.
:PD.The public&colon. every user with no other authority.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGAUT/DTAAUT'.New data authorities (DTAAUT)
:P.The data authorities&colon. read, add, update, delete and execute.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*EXCLUDE:EPK.
:PD.No authority&colon. the object cannot be used.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *RWX, *RX, *RW, *WX, *R, *W, *X, *AUTL.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGAUT/OBJAUT'.New object authorities (OBJAUT)
:P.The object authorities&colon. operational, management, existence,
alter and reference.
:P.Up to 4 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*OBJEXIST:EPK.
:PD.Object existence authority.
:PT.:PK.*OBJMGT:EPK.
:PD.Object management authority.
:PT.:PK.*OBJALTER:EPK.
:PD.Object alter authority.
:PT.:PK.*OBJREF:EPK.
:PD.Object reference authority.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGAUT/AUTL'.Authorization list (AUTL)
:P.The authorization list that secures the object.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGAUT/SYMLNK'.Symbolic link (SYMLNK)
:P.Whether to symbolic link.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGAUT/SUBTREE'.Directory subtree (SUBTREE)
:P.Whether the objects in the subdirectories are included.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.The objects of the directory only.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.The directory and everything below it.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CHGAUTLE.Change Auth List Entry (CHGAUTLE)
:P.Use the Change Auth List Entry (CHGAUTLE) command to change the
authority of users already on an authorization list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGAUTLE/AUTL'.Authorization list (AUTL)
:P.The authorization list that secures the object.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGAUTLE/USER'.Users (USER)
:P.The users for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:P.Up to 50 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*PUBLIC:EPK.
:PD.The public&colon. every user with no other authority.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGAUTLE/AUT'.Authority (AUT)
:P.The authority the public (users with no private authority and no
group authority) gets to the new object.
:P.Up to 11 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*USE:EPK.
:PD.Use authority&colon. the object can be read and run but not changed.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All authority&colon. the user can do anything with the object except
change its owner or what secures it.
:PT.:PK.*CHANGE:EPK.
:PD.Change authority&colon. all data authorities and operational
authority. The object can be used and its contents changed.
:PT.:PK.*EXCLUDE:EPK.
:PD.No authority&colon. the object cannot be used.
:PT.:PK.*OBJALTER:EPK.
:PD.Object alter authority.
:PT.:PK.*OBJEXIST:EPK.
:PD.Object existence authority.
:PT.:PK.*OBJMGT:EPK.
:PD.Object management authority.
:PT.:PK.*OBJOPR:EPK.
:PD.Object operational authority.
:PT.:PK.*OBJREF:EPK.
:PD.Object reference authority.
:PT.:PK.*ADD:EPK.
:PD.The new entries are added to what is there.
:PT.:PK.*DLT:EPK.
:PD.Delete authority.
:PT.:PK.*EXECUTE:EPK.
:PD.Execute authority.
:PT.:PK.*READ:EPK.
:PD.Read authority.
:PT.:PK.*UPD:EPK.
:PD.Update authority.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *AUTLMGT.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CHGDSTPWD.Change IBM Service Tools Pwd (CHGDSTPWD)
:P.Use the Change IBM Service Tools Pwd (CHGDSTPWD) command to put
service tools user ID QSECOFR back to its shipped, expired password and
enable it; only QSECOFR may run it.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGDSTPWD/PASSWORD'.Password (PASSWORD)
:P.The password.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *DEFAULT.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CHGFCNUSG.Change Function Usage (CHGFCNUSG)
:P.The Change Function Usage (CHGFCNUSG) command works with a function's
default, its *ALLOBJ use, a profile's usage.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGFCNUSG/FCNID'.Function ID (FCNID)
:P.The function ID for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 30 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGFCNUSG/USER'.User (USER)
:P.The user for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGFCNUSG/USAGE'.Usage (USAGE)
:P.The usage for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *ALLOWED, *DENIED.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGFCNUSG/DEFAULT'.Default authority (DEFAULT)
:P.The default authority for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *ALLOWED, *DENIED.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGFCNUSG/ALLOBJAUT'.*ALLOBJ special authority (ALLOBJAUT)
:P.The *ALLOBJ special authority for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *USED, *NOTUSED.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CHGOBJAUD.Change Object Auditing (CHGOBJAUD)
:P.Use the Change Object Auditing (CHGOBJAUD) command to set the
auditing value of objects.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGOBJAUD/OBJ'.Object (OBJ)
:P.The object or objects the command works on, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PK.*USRLIBL:EPK.
:PD.The libraries of the user part of the library list.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*ALLUSR:EPK.
:PD.Every user library&colon. libraries whose names do not start with Q,
and the Q libraries that hold user data (QGPL, QUSRSYS and the like).
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGOBJAUD/OBJTYPE'.Object type (OBJTYPE)
:P.The type or types of the objects the command works on.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
