:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGOBJPGP/NEWPGP'.New primary group (NEWPGP)
:P.The new primary group for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGOBJPGP/ASPDEV'.ASP device (ASPDEV)
:P.The auxiliary storage pool device the command works in&colon. the
system ASP and basic user ASPs, or an independent ASP group.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*SYSBAS:EPK.
:PD.The system ASP and the basic user ASPs.
:PT.:PK.*CURASPGRP:EPK.
:PD.The ASP group of the job's current thread.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGOBJPGP/PGPAUT'.New primary group authority (PGPAUT)
:P.The new primary group authority for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*PRIVATE:EPK.
:PD.Private authorities.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*CHANGE:EPK.
:PD.Change authority&colon. all data authorities and operational
authority. The object can be used and its contents changed.
:PT.:PK.*USE:EPK.
:PD.Use authority&colon. the object can be read and run but not changed.
:PT.:PK.*EXCLUDE:EPK.
:PD.No authority&colon. the object cannot be used.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *OLDPGP.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGOBJPGP/RVKOLDAUT'.Revoke old primary group (RVKOLDAUT)
:P.Whether to revoke old primary group.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CHGOWN.Change Owner (CHGOWN)
:P.Use the Change Owner (CHGOWN) command to give an IFS object a new
owner.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGOWN/OBJ'.Object (OBJ)
:P.The object or objects the command works on, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGOWN/NEWOWN'.New owner (NEWOWN)
:P.The new owner for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGOWN/RVKOLDAUT'.Revoke current owner authority (RVKOLDAUT)
:P.Whether to revoke current owner authority.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGOWN/SYMLNK'.Symbolic link (SYMLNK)
:P.Whether to symbolic link.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGOWN/SUBTREE'.Directory subtree (SUBTREE)
:P.Whether the objects in the subdirectories are included.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.The objects of the directory only.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.The directory and everything below it.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CHGPGP.Change Primary Group (CHGPGP)
:P.Use the Change Primary Group (CHGPGP) command to give an IFS object a
new primary group.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPGP/OBJ'.Object (OBJ)
:P.The object or objects the command works on, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPGP/NEWPGP'.New primary group (NEWPGP)
:P.The new primary group for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPGP/DTAAUT'.New data authority (DTAAUT)
:P.The data authorities&colon. read, add, update, delete and execute.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*PRIVATE:EPK.
:PD.Private authorities.
:PT.:PK.*EXCLUDE:EPK.
:PD.No authority&colon. the object cannot be used.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *OLDPGP, *RWX, *RX, *RW, *WX, *R, *W, *X.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPGP/OBJAUT'.New object authority (OBJAUT)
:P.The object authorities&colon. operational, management, existence,
alter and reference.
:P.Up to 4 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*OBJEXIST:EPK.
:PD.Object existence authority.
:PT.:PK.*OBJMGT:EPK.
:PD.Object management authority.
:PT.:PK.*OBJALTER:EPK.
:PD.Object alter authority.
:PT.:PK.*OBJREF:EPK.
:PD.Object reference authority.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPGP/RVKOLDAUT'.Revoke old authority (RVKOLDAUT)
:P.Whether to revoke old authority.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPGP/SYMLNK'.Symbolic link (SYMLNK)
:P.Whether to symbolic link.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGPGP/SUBTREE'.Directory subtree (SUBTREE)
:P.Whether the objects in the subdirectories are included.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.The objects of the directory only.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.The directory and everything below it.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CHGPWD.Change Password (CHGPWD)
:P.Use the Change Password (CHGPWD) command to change the password of
the signed-on user; the old and new passwords are entered on a screen,
so the command has no parameters.
:P.The command has no parameters.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CHGSECA.Change Security Attributes (CHGSECA)
:P.Use the Change Security Attributes (CHGSECA) command to where
generated user and group ID numbers start.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGSECA/UID'.User ID number (UID)
:P.The user ID number for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 10 digits. The value must be from 101 to
4294967294.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGSECA/GID'.Group ID number (GID)
:P.The group ID number for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a number of up to 10 digits. The value must be from 101 to
4294967294.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CHGSECAUD.Change Security Auditing (CHGSECAUD)
:P.Use the Change Security Auditing (CHGSECAUD) command to set the
auditing system values and make sure QAUDJRN and its receiver exist.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGSECAUD/QAUDCTL'.Auditing control (QAUDCTL)
:P.The auditing control for this command.
:P.Up to 3 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *AUDLVL, *OBJAUD, *NOQTEMP.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGSECAUD/QAUDLVL'.Auditing level (QAUDLVL)
:P.The auditing level for this command.
:P.Up to 32 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*DELETE:EPK.
:PD.Deleted.
:PT.:PK.*OBJMGT:EPK.
:PD.Object management authority.
:PT.:PK.*SAVRST:EPK.
:PD.Save and restore operations.
:PT.:PK.*SERVICE:EPK.
:PD.Service.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *DFTSET, *ATNEVT, *AUTFAIL, *CREATE, *JOBBAS,
*JOBCHGUSR, *JOBDTA, *NETBAS, *NETCLU, *NETCMN, *NETFAIL, *NETSCK,
*NETSECURE, *NETTELSVR, *NETUDP, *OFCSRV, *OPTICAL, *PGMADP, *PGMFAIL,
*PRTDTA, *PTFOBJ, *PTFOPR, *SECCFG, *SECDIRSRV, *SECIPC, *SECNAS,
*SECRUN, *SECSCKD, *SECURITY, *SECVFY, *SECVLDL, *SPLFDTA, *SYSMGT,
*AUDLVL2.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGSECAUD/QAUDLVL2'.Auditing level extension (QAUDLVL2)
:P.The auditing level extension for this command.
:P.Up to 32 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*DELETE:EPK.
:PD.Deleted.
:PT.:PK.*OBJMGT:EPK.
:PD.Object management authority.
:PT.:PK.*SAVRST:EPK.
:PD.Save and restore operations.
:PT.:PK.*SERVICE:EPK.
:PD.Service.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *ATNEVT, *AUTFAIL, *CREATE, *JOBBAS, *JOBCHGUSR,
*JOBDTA, *NETBAS, *NETCLU, *NETCMN, *NETFAIL, *NETSCK, *NETSECURE,
*NETTELSVR, *NETUDP, *OFCSRV, *OPTICAL, *PGMADP, *PGMFAIL, *PRTDTA,
*PTFOBJ, *PTFOPR, *SECCFG, *SECDIRSRV, *SECIPC, *SECNAS, *SECRUN,
*SECSCKD, *SECURITY, *SECVFY, *SECVLDL, *SPLFDTA, *SYSMGT.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGSECAUD/JRNRCV'.Initial journal receiver (JRNRCV)
:P.The journal receiver, by name and library.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*GEN:EPK.
:PD.Generated by the system.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CHGUSRAUD.Change User Auditing (CHGUSRAUD)
:P.Use the Change User Auditing (CHGUSRAUD) command to set the object
and action auditing of user profiles.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGUSRAUD/USRPRF'.User profile (USRPRF)
:P.The user profile the command uses.
:P.A value is required.
:P.Up to 50 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGUSRAUD/OBJAUD'.Object auditing value (OBJAUD)
:P.The object auditing value for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*CHANGE:EPK.
:PD.Change authority&colon. all data authorities and operational
authority. The object can be used and its contents changed.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGUSRAUD/AUDLVL'.User action auditing (AUDLVL)
:P.The user action auditing for this command.
:P.Up to 32 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*CMD:EPK.
:PD.The value of the command.
:PT.:PK.*DELETE:EPK.
:PD.Deleted.
:PT.:PK.*OBJMGT:EPK.
:PD.Object management authority.
:PT.:PK.*SAVRST:EPK.
:PD.Save and restore operations.
:PT.:PK.*SERVICE:EPK.
:PD.Service.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *ATNEVT, *CREATE, *JOBBAS, *JOBCHGUSR, *JOBDTA,
*NETBAS, *NETCLU, *NETCMN, *NETFAIL, *NETSCK, *NETSECURE, *NETTELSVR,
*NETUDP, *OFCSRV, *OPTICAL, *PGMADP, *PGMFAIL, *PRTDTA, *PTFOBJ,
*PTFOPR, *SECCFG, *SECDIRSRV, *SECIPC, *SECNAS, *SECRUN, *SECSCKD,
*SECURITY, *SECVFY, *SECVLDL, *SPLFDTA, *SYSMGT.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CHGUSRPRF.Change User Profile (CHGUSRPRF)
:P.Use the Change User Profile (CHGUSRPRF) command to change a user
profile; every attribute defaults to *SAME.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGUSRPRF/USRPRF'.User profile (USRPRF)
:P.The user profile the command uses.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGUSRPRF/PASSWORD'.User password (PASSWORD)
:P.The password.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*USRPRF:EPK.
:PD.The value of the user profile the job runs under.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 128 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGUSRPRF/PWDEXP'.Set password to expired (PWDEXP)
:P.The set password to expired for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGUSRPRF/STATUS'.Status (STATUS)
:P.The status for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *ENABLED, *DISABLED.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGUSRPRF/USRCLS'.User class (USRCLS)
:P.The user class&colon. security officer, security administrator,
programmer, system operator or user.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*USER:EPK.
:PD.The user.
:PT.:PK.*SYSOPR:EPK.
:PD.The system operator message queue, QSYSOPR.
:PT.:PK.*PGMR:EPK.
:PD.Programmer.
:PT.:PK.*SECADM:EPK.
:PD.Security administrator.
:PT.:PK.*SECOFR:EPK.
:PD.Security officer.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGUSRPRF/ASTLVL'.Assistance level (ASTLVL)
:P.The assistance level the user's displays show&colon. basic
(Operational Assistant), intermediate (the system displays) or advanced.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*SYSVAL:EPK.
:PD.The value of the system value that holds the default.
:PT.:PK.*BASIC:EPK.
:PD.Basic.
:PT.:PK.*INTERMED:EPK.
:PD.Intermediate assistance&colon. the system displays.
:PT.:PK.*ADVANCED:EPK.
:PD.Advanced assistance&colon. the system displays with more on each and
fewer keys shown.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGUSRPRF/CURLIB'.Current library (CURLIB)
:P.The current library of the job&colon. the library searched first by
name (after the system part of the library list) and where *CURLIB puts
new objects.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *CRTDFT.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGUSRPRF/INLPGM'.Initial program to call (INLPGM)
:P.The initial program to call for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGUSRPRF/INLMNU'.Initial menu (INLMNU)
:P.The initial menu for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *SIGNOFF.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGUSRPRF/LMTCPB'.Limit capabilities (LMTCPB)
:P.The limit capabilities for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *PARTIAL.
