:P.The type of authority for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:P.Also accepted&colon. *OBJECT, *FIELD.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=DSPSECA.Display Security Attributes (DSPSECA)
:P.The Display Security Attributes (DSPSECA) command works with the
security attributes&colon. next ID numbers, levels, DST flags.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPSECA/OUTPUT'.Output (OUTPUT)
:P.Where the command sends what it produces&colon. to the display of an
interactive job, or to a spooled file of the job's printer file. Some
commands can also write it to a database file.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*:EPK.
:PD.The output is shown at the display of an interactive job, and
printed for a batch job.
:PT.:PK.*PRINT:EPK.
:PD.The output is printed with the job's spooled output.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=DSPSECAUD.Display Security Auditing (DSPSECAUD)
:P.Use the Display Security Auditing (DSPSECAUD) command to show the
auditing system values and the audit journal.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPSECAUD/OUTPUT'.Output (OUTPUT)
:P.Where the command sends what it produces&colon. to the display of an
