:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=PRTQAUT.Print Queue Authority (PRTQAUT)
:P.Use the Print Queue Authority (PRTQAUT) command to print the
authorities to the job and output queues of a library.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='PRTQAUT/LIB'.Library (LIB)
:P.The library for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*ALLUSR:EPK.
:PD.Every user library&colon. libraries whose names do not start with Q,
and the Q libraries that hold user data (QGPL, QUSRSYS and the like).
:PT.:PK.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=PRTSBSDAUT.Print Subsystem Desc Auth (PRTSBSDAUT)
:P.Use the Print Subsystem Desc Auth (PRTSBSDAUT) command to print the
subsystem descriptions whose entries name a default user.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='PRTSBSDAUT/LIB'.Library (LIB)
:P.The library for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*ALLUSR:EPK.
:PD.Every user library&colon. libraries whose names do not start with Q,
and the Q libraries that hold user data (QGPL, QUSRSYS and the like).
:PT.:PK.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=PRTSYSSECA.Print System Security Attr (PRTSYSSECA)
:P.Use the Print System Security Attr (PRTSYSSECA) command to print the
security system values and network attributes against their recommended
settings.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='PRTSYSSECA/TYPE'.Type of information (TYPE)
:P.The type of information for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*SYSVAL:EPK.
:PD.The value of the system value that holds the default.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *NETA.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=PRTUSROBJ.Print User Objects (PRTUSROBJ)
:P.Use the Print User Objects (PRTUSROBJ) command to print the
user-created objects in a library.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='PRTUSROBJ/LIB'.Library (LIB)
:P.The library for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*ALLUSR:EPK.
:PD.Every user library&colon. libraries whose names do not start with Q,
and the Q libraries that hold user data (QGPL, QUSRSYS and the like).
:PT.:PK.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=PRTUSRPRF.Print User Profile (PRTUSRPRF)
:P.Use the Print User Profile (PRTUSRPRF) command to print a report on
the user profiles selected.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='PRTUSRPRF/TYPE'.Type of information (TYPE)
:P.The type of information for this command.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *AUTINFO, *ENVINFO, *PWDINFO, *PWDLVL.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='PRTUSRPRF/SELECT'.Select by (SELECT)
:P.The select by for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *USRCLS, *SPCAUT, *MISMATCH.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='PRTUSRPRF/USRCLS'.User classes (USRCLS)
:P.The user class&colon. security officer, security administrator,
programmer, system operator or user.
:P.Up to 5 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*USER:EPK.
:PD.The user.
:PT.:PK.*SYSOPR:EPK.
:PD.The system operator message queue, QSYSOPR.
:PT.:PK.*PGMR:EPK.
:PD.Programmer.
:PT.:PK.*SECADM:EPK.
:PD.Security administrator.
:PT.:PK.*SECOFR:EPK.
:PD.Security officer.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='PRTUSRPRF/SPCAUT'.Special authorities (SPCAUT)
:P.The special authorities the user profile has.
:P.Up to 8 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALLOBJ:EPK.
:PD.All object special authority.
:PT.:PK.*AUDIT:EPK.
:PD.Audit special authority.
:PT.:PK.*IOSYSCFG:EPK.
:PD.Input/output system configuration special authority.
:PT.:PK.*JOBCTL:EPK.
:PD.Job control special authority.
:PT.:PK.*SAVSYS:EPK.
:PD.Save system special authority.
:PT.:PK.*SECADM:EPK.
:PD.Security administrator.
:PT.:PK.*SERVICE:EPK.
:PD.Service.
:PT.:PK.*SPLCTL:EPK.
:PD.Spool control special authority.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=QSADDAPPID.Add Certificate Application (QSADDAPPID)
:P.Use the Add Certificate Application (QSADDAPPID) command to register
an application ID for certificates.
:P.This command is a QS/400 extension.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSADDAPPID/APPID'.Application ID (APPID)
:P.The application identifier.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 100 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSADDAPPID/TYPE'.Application type (TYPE)
:P.The application type for this command.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *SERVER, *CLIENT.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSADDAPPID/TEXT'.Text (TEXT)
:P.A short description of the object, up to 50 characters, shown by the
work-with and display commands next to its name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.No text.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=QSASNCRT.Assign Certificate (QSASNCRT)
:P.Use the Assign Certificate (QSASNCRT) command to assign a certificate
of *SYSTEM to an application ID.
:P.This command is a QS/400 extension.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSASNCRT/APPID'.Application ID (APPID)
:P.The application identifier.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 100 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSASNCRT/LABEL'.Certificate label (LABEL)
:P.The label of the file on the volume.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 64 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=QSCHGAPPID.Change Certificate Application (QSCHGAPPID)
:P.Use the Change Certificate Application (QSCHGAPPID) command to change
an application ID's client authentication, CA trust list or text.
:P.This command is a QS/400 extension.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSCHGAPPID/APPID'.Application ID (APPID)
:P.The application identifier.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 100 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSCHGAPPID/CLTAUTH'.Client authentication (CLTAUTH)
:P.The client authentication for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *OPTIONAL, *REQUIRED.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSCHGAPPID/CATRUST'.Trusted CA labels (CATRUST)
:P.The trusted CA labels for this command.
:P.Up to 50 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 64 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSCHGAPPID/TEXT'.Text (TEXT)
:P.A short description of the object, up to 50 characters, shown by the
work-with and display commands next to its name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The text does not change.
:PT.:PK.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.No text.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=QSCHGCRT.Change Certificate (QSCHGCRT)
:P.Use the Change Certificate (QSCHGCRT) command to change a
certificate's label, trust, default or text.
:P.This command is a QS/400 extension.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSCHGCRT/LABEL'.Certificate label (LABEL)
:P.The label of the file on the volume.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 64 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSCHGCRT/KEYSTORE'.Certificate store (KEYSTORE)
:P.The certificate store for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SYSTEM:EPK.
:PD.The system.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 256 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *LCLCA.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSCHGCRT/PASSWORD'.Store password (PASSWORD)
:P.The password.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 128 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *STASH.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSCHGCRT/NEWLABEL'.New label (NEWLABEL)
:P.The new label for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 64 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSCHGCRT/TRUST'.Trusted CA (TRUST)
:P.The trusted CA for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSCHGCRT/DFTCRT'.Make the store default (DFTCRT)
:P.Whether to make the store default.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSCHGCRT/TEXT'.Text (TEXT)
:P.A short description of the object, up to 50 characters, shown by the
work-with and display commands next to its name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The text does not change.
:PT.:PK.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.No text.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=QSCHKCRT.Check Certificate Expiry (QSCHKCRT)
:P.Use the Check Certificate Expiry (QSCHKCRT) command to check the
system's certificates for expiry now; warnings go to QSYSOPR.
:P.This command is a QS/400 extension.
:P.The command has no parameters.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=QSCRTCRT.Create Certificate (QSCRTCRT)
:P.Use the Create Certificate (QSCRTCRT) command to create a certificate
with a new key&colon. self-signed, signed by the local CA, or a request.
:P.This command is a QS/400 extension.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSCRTCRT/LABEL'.Certificate label (LABEL)
:P.The label of the file on the volume.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 64 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSCRTCRT/CN'.Common name (CN)
:P.The common name for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 64 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSCRTCRT/KEYSTORE'.Certificate store (KEYSTORE)
:P.The certificate store for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SYSTEM:EPK.
:PD.The system.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 256 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *LCLCA.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSCRTCRT/PASSWORD'.Store password (PASSWORD)
:P.The password.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 128 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *STASH.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSCRTCRT/SIGNER'.Signed by (SIGNER)
:P.The signed by for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SELF:EPK.
:PD.Itself.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *LCLCA, *CSR.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSCRTCRT/USAGE'.Certificate use (USAGE)
:P.The certificate use for this command.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *SERVER, *CLIENT.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSCRTCRT/ORG'.Organization (ORG)
:P.The organization for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 64 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSCRTCRT/ORGUNIT'.Organizational unit (ORGUNIT)
:P.The organizational unit for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 64 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSCRTCRT/LOCALITY'.Locality (LOCALITY)
:P.The locality for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 64 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSCRTCRT/STATE'.State or province (STATE)
:P.The state or province for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 64 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSCRTCRT/COUNTRY'.Country code (COUNTRY)
:P.The country code for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 5 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSCRTCRT/ALTNAME'.Alternative names (ALTNAME)
:P.The alternative names for this command.
:P.Up to 10 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 255 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *CN.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSCRTCRT/KEYALG'.Key algorithm (KEYALG)
:P.The key algorithm for this command.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *ECDSAP256, *ECDSAP384, *RSA2048, *RSA3072,
*RSA4096.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSCRTCRT/VALIDITY'.Validity in days (VALIDITY)
:P.The validity in days for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 7300.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 365 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSCRTCRT/CSR'.Request stream file (CSR)
:P.The request stream file for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 256 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSCRTCRT/LCLCAPWD'.Local CA password (LCLCAPWD)
:P.The local CA password for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 128 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *STASH.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSCRTCRT/TEXT'.Text (TEXT)
:P.A short description of the object, up to 50 characters, shown by the
work-with and display commands next to its name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.No text.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=QSCRTCRTS.Create Certificate Store (QSCRTCRTS)
:P.Use the Create Certificate Store (QSCRTCRTS) command to create a
certificate store.
:P.This command is a QS/400 extension.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSCRTCRTS/KEYSTORE'.Certificate store (KEYSTORE)
:P.The certificate store for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*SYSTEM:EPK.
:PD.The system.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 256 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *LCLCA.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSCRTCRTS/PASSWORD'.Store password (PASSWORD)
:P.The password.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 128 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSCRTCRTS/STASH'.Keep the password for servers (STASH)
:P.Whether to keep the password for servers.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSCRTCRTS/ROOTS'.Add the shipped root CAs (ROOTS)
:P.Whether to add the shipped root CAs.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSCRTCRTS/CN'.Local CA common name (CN)
:P.The local CA common name for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*GEN:EPK.
:PD.Generated by the system.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 64 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSCRTCRTS/ORG'.Organization (ORG)
:P.The organization for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 64 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSCRTCRTS/ORGUNIT'.Organizational unit (ORGUNIT)
:P.The organizational unit for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 64 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSCRTCRTS/LOCALITY'.Locality (LOCALITY)
:P.The locality for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 64 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSCRTCRTS/STATE'.State or province (STATE)
:P.The state or province for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 64 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSCRTCRTS/COUNTRY'.Country code (COUNTRY)
:P.The country code for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 5 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSCRTCRTS/KEYALG'.Key algorithm (KEYALG)
:P.The key algorithm for this command.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *ECDSAP256, *ECDSAP384, *RSA2048, *RSA3072,
*RSA4096.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSCRTCRTS/VALIDITY'.Local CA validity in days (VALIDITY)
:P.The local CA validity in days for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 7300.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 3650 is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=QSDLTCRT.Delete Certificate (QSDLTCRT)
:P.Use the Delete Certificate (QSDLTCRT) command to remove a certificate
from a store.
:P.This command is a QS/400 extension.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSDLTCRT/LABEL'.Certificate label (LABEL)
:P.The label of the file on the volume.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 64 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSDLTCRT/KEYSTORE'.Certificate store (KEYSTORE)
:P.The certificate store for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SYSTEM:EPK.
:PD.The system.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 256 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *LCLCA.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSDLTCRT/PASSWORD'.Store password (PASSWORD)
:P.The password.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 128 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *STASH.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=QSDLTCRTS.Delete Certificate Store (QSDLTCRTS)
:P.Use the Delete Certificate Store (QSDLTCRTS) command to delete a
certificate store and its stash.
:P.This command is a QS/400 extension.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSDLTCRTS/KEYSTORE'.Certificate store (KEYSTORE)
:P.The certificate store for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*SYSTEM:EPK.
:PD.The system.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 256 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *LCLCA.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSDLTCRTS/PASSWORD'.Store password (PASSWORD)
:P.The password.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 128 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *STASH.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=QSEXPCRT.Export Certificate (QSEXPCRT)
:P.Use the Export Certificate (QSEXPCRT) command to export a
certificate, with its key, or a request to a stream file.
:P.This command is a QS/400 extension.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSEXPCRT/LABEL'.Certificate label (LABEL)
:P.The label of the file on the volume.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 64 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSEXPCRT/TOSTMF'.Stream file to write (TOSTMF)
:P.The stream file to write for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSEXPCRT/KEYSTORE'.Certificate store (KEYSTORE)
:P.The certificate store for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SYSTEM:EPK.
:PD.The system.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 256 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *LCLCA.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSEXPCRT/PASSWORD'.Store password (PASSWORD)
:P.The password.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 128 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *STASH.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSEXPCRT/FORMAT'.File format (FORMAT)
:P.The file format for this command.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *PEM, *PKCS12, *CSR.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSEXPCRT/INCKEY'.Include the private key (INCKEY)
:P.Whether to include the private key.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSEXPCRT/EXPPWD'.File password (EXPPWD)
:P.The file password for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 128 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSEXPCRT/REPLACE'.Replace the stream file (REPLACE)
:P.Whether an existing object of the same name is replaced. A replaced
object is moved to library QRPLOBJ when it is in use.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.The command ends with a message when an object of the same name
exists.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.An existing object of the same name is replaced.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=QSIMPCRT.Import Certificate (QSIMPCRT)
:P.Use the Import Certificate (QSIMPCRT) command to import certificates
and keys from a PEM or PKCS#12 stream file.
:P.This command is a QS/400 extension.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSIMPCRT/FROMSTMF'.Stream file to import (FROMSTMF)
:P.The stream file to import for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSIMPCRT/LABEL'.Certificate label (LABEL)
:P.The label of the file on the volume.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 64 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSIMPCRT/KEYSTORE'.Certificate store (KEYSTORE)
:P.The certificate store for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SYSTEM:EPK.
:PD.The system.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 256 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *LCLCA.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSIMPCRT/PASSWORD'.Store password (PASSWORD)
:P.The password.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 128 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *STASH.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSIMPCRT/FORMAT'.File format (FORMAT)
:P.The file format for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*AUTO:EPK.
:PD.Chosen automatically.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *PEM, *PKCS12.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSIMPCRT/IMPPWD'.File password (IMPPWD)
:P.The file password for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 128 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSIMPCRT/TRUST'.Trust imported CAs (TRUST)
:P.Whether to trust imported CAs.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=QSRMVAPPID.Remove Certificate Application (QSRMVAPPID)
:P.Use the Remove Certificate Application (QSRMVAPPID) command to remove
an application ID a user registered.
:P.This command is a QS/400 extension.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSRMVAPPID/APPID'.Application ID (APPID)
:P.The application identifier.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 100 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=QSSECCHK.Check System Security (QSSECCHK)
:P.Use the Check System Security (QSSECCHK) command to check the running
system against the security model and print pass, warning or failure for
each check.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSSECCHK/OUTPUT'.Output (OUTPUT)
:P.Where the command sends what it produces&colon. to the display of an
interactive job, or to a spooled file of the job's printer file. Some
commands can also write it to a database file.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*:EPK.
:PD.The output is shown at the display of an interactive job, and
printed for a batch job.
:PT.:PK DEF.*PRINT:EPK.
:PD.The output is printed with the job's spooled output.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=QSWRKAPPID.Work with Cert Applications (QSWRKAPPID)
:P.Use the Work with Cert Applications (QSWRKAPPID) command to work with
the certificate application IDs.
:P.This command is a QS/400 extension.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSWRKAPPID/APPID'.Application ID (APPID)
:P.The application identifier.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 100 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=QSWRKCRT.Work with Certificates (QSWRKCRT)
:P.Use the Work with Certificates (QSWRKCRT) command to work with the
certificates of a store.
:P.This command is a QS/400 extension.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSWRKCRT/KEYSTORE'.Certificate store (KEYSTORE)
:P.The certificate store for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SYSTEM:EPK.
:PD.The system.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 256 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *LCLCA.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSWRKCRT/PASSWORD'.Store password (PASSWORD)
:P.The password.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 128 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *STASH.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=RMVAUTLE.Remove Auth List Entry (RMVAUTLE)
:P.Use the Remove Auth List Entry (RMVAUTLE) command to remove users
from an authorization list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVAUTLE/AUTL'.Authorization list (AUTL)
:P.The authorization list that secures the object.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVAUTLE/USER'.Users (USER)
:P.The users for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:P.Up to 50 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*PUBLIC:EPK.
:PD.The public&colon. every user with no other authority.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=RVKOBJAUT.Revoke Object Authority (RVKOBJAUT)
:P.Use the Revoke Object Authority (RVKOBJAUT) command to take authority
to objects away from users, the public or an authorization list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RVKOBJAUT/OBJ'.Object (OBJ)
:P.The object or objects the command works on, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PK.*USRLIBL:EPK.
:PD.The libraries of the user part of the library list.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*ALLUSR:EPK.
:PD.Every user library&colon. libraries whose names do not start with Q,
and the Q libraries that hold user data (QGPL, QUSRSYS and the like).
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RVKOBJAUT/OBJTYPE'.Object type (OBJTYPE)
:P.The type or types of the objects the command works on.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
