:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RVKOBJAUT/ASPDEV'.ASP device (ASPDEV)
:P.The auxiliary storage pool device the command works in&colon. the
system ASP and basic user ASPs, or an independent ASP group.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*SYSBAS:EPK.
:PD.The system ASP and the basic user ASPs.
:PT.:PK.*CURASPGRP:EPK.
:PD.The ASP group of the job's current thread.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RVKOBJAUT/USER'.Users (USER)
:P.The users for this command.
:P.Up to 50 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*PUBLIC:EPK.
:PD.The public&colon. every user with no other authority.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RVKOBJAUT/AUTL'.Authorization list (AUTL)
:P.The authorization list that secures the object.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RVKOBJAUT/AUT'.Authority (AUT)
:P.The authority the public (users with no private authority and no
group authority) gets to the new object.
:P.Up to 10 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CHANGE:EPK.
:PD.Change authority&colon. all data authorities and operational
authority. The object can be used and its contents changed.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All authority&colon. the user can do anything with the object except
change its owner or what secures it.
:PT.:PK.*USE:EPK.
:PD.Use authority&colon. the object can be read and run but not changed.
:PT.:PK.*EXCLUDE:EPK.
:PD.No authority&colon. the object cannot be used.
:PT.:PK.*OBJALTER:EPK.
:PD.Object alter authority.
:PT.:PK.*OBJEXIST:EPK.
:PD.Object existence authority.
:PT.:PK.*OBJMGT:EPK.
:PD.Object management authority.
:PT.:PK.*OBJOPR:EPK.
:PD.Object operational authority.
:PT.:PK.*OBJREF:EPK.
:PD.Object reference authority.
:PT.:PK.*ADD:EPK.
:PD.The new entries are added to what is there.
:PT.:PK.*DLT:EPK.
:PD.Delete authority.
:PT.:PK.*EXECUTE:EPK.
:PD.Execute authority.
:PT.:PK.*READ:EPK.
:PD.Read authority.
:PT.:PK.*UPD:EPK.
:PD.Update authority.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *AUTL.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=STRPASTHR.Start Pass-Through (STRPASTHR)
:P.Use the Start Pass-Through (STRPASTHR) command to 5250 display
station pass-through runs over APPC, which QS/400 does not have&colon.
no remote location is found (CPF8933).
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRPASTHR/RMTLOCNAME'.Remote location (RMTLOCNAME)
:P.The remote location name of the system at the other end of the
connection.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 8 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *CNNDEV.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRPASTHR/VRTCTL'.Virtual controller (VRTCTL)
:P.The virtual controller for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRPASTHR/VRTDEV'.Virtual display device (VRTDEV)
:P.The virtual display device for this command.
:P.Up to 32 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRPASTHR/MODE'.Mode (MODE)
:P.The mode for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NETATR:EPK.
:PD.The value of the network attributes (DSPNETA).
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 8 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRPASTHR/LCLLOCNAME'.Local location (LCLLOCNAME)
:P.The local location name this system uses on the connection.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LOC:EPK.
:PD.The location.
:PT.:PK.*NETATR:EPK.
:PD.The value of the network attributes (DSPNETA).
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 8 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRPASTHR/RMTNETID'.Remote network identifier (RMTNETID)
:P.The network identifier of the remote location.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LOC:EPK.
:PD.The location.
:PT.:PK.*NETATR:EPK.
:PD.The value of the network attributes (DSPNETA).
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 8 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRPASTHR/SRQ10PGM'.System request program (SRQ10PGM)
:P.The system request program for this command.
:PARML.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *SRQMNU.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRPASTHR/CNNDEV'.APPC device (CNNDEV)
:P.The APPC device for this command.
:P.Up to 16 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LOC:EPK.
:PD.The location.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRPASTHR/RMTUSER'.User profile (RMTUSER)
:P.The user profile for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*CURRENT:EPK.
:PD.The current one.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRPASTHR/RMTPWD'.User password (RMTPWD)
:P.The user password for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 128 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRPASTHR/RMTINLPGM'.Initial program to call (RMTINLPGM)
:P.The initial program to call for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *RMTUSRPRF.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRPASTHR/RMTINLMNU'.Initial menu (RMTINLMNU)
:P.The initial menu for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *RMTUSRPRF, *SIGNOFF.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRPASTHR/RMTCURLIB'.Current library (RMTCURLIB)
:P.The current library for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *RMTUSRPRF.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRPASTHR/PASTHRSCN'.Display option (PASTHRSCN)
:P.Whether to display option.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=WRKAUT.Work with Authority (WRKAUT)
:P.The Work with Authority (WRKAUT) command works with an IFS object's
authorities, with options to change them.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKAUT/OBJ'.Object (OBJ)
:P.The object or objects the command works on, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKAUT/SYMLNK'.Symbolic link (SYMLNK)
:P.Whether to symbolic link.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=WRKAUTL.Work with Authorization Lists (WRKAUTL)
:P.Use the Work with Authorization Lists (WRKAUTL) command to list
authorization lists and work with them.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKAUTL/AUTL'.Authorization list (AUTL)
:P.The authorization list that secures the object.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKAUTL/OUTPUT'.Output (OUTPUT)
:P.Where the command sends what it produces&colon. to the display of an
interactive job, or to a spooled file of the job's printer file. Some
commands can also write it to a database file.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*:EPK.
:PD.The output is shown at the display of an interactive job, and
printed for a batch job.
:PT.:PK.*PRINT:EPK.
:PD.The output is printed with the job's spooled output.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=WRKFCNUSG.Work with Function Usage (WRKFCNUSG)
:P.The Work with Function Usage (WRKFCNUSG) command works with the
function usage registry, options 2 and 5.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKFCNUSG/FCNID'.Function ID (FCNID)
:P.The function ID for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 30 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=WRKOBJOWN.Work with Objects by Owner (WRKOBJOWN)
:P.Use the Work with Objects by Owner (WRKOBJOWN) command to list the
objects a user owns and work with them.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKOBJOWN/USRPRF'.User profile (USRPRF)
:P.The user profile the command uses.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CURRENT:EPK.
:PD.The current one.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKOBJOWN/OBJTYPE'.Object type (OBJTYPE)
:P.The type or types of the objects the command works on.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
