:HELP NAME='WRKOBJOWN/OUTPUT'.Output (OUTPUT)
:P.Where the command sends what it produces&colon. to the display of an
interactive job, or to a spooled file of the job's printer file. Some
commands can also write it to a database file.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*:EPK.
:PD.The output is shown at the display of an interactive job, and
printed for a batch job.
:PT.:PK.*PRINT:EPK.
:PD.The output is printed with the job's spooled output.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=WRKOBJPGP.Work with Objects by Primary Group (WRKOBJPGP)
:P.Use the Work with Objects by Primary Group (WRKOBJPGP) command to
list the objects a group profile is the primary group of.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKOBJPGP/PGP'.Primary group (PGP)
:P.The primary group for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKOBJPGP/OBJTYPE'.Object type (OBJTYPE)
:P.The type or types of the objects the command works on.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=WRKUSRPRF.Work with User Profiles (WRKUSRPRF)
:P.Use the Work with User Profiles (WRKUSRPRF) command to list user
profiles and work with them.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKUSRPRF/USRPRF'.User profile (USRPRF)
:P.The user profile the command uses.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKUSRPRF/OUTPUT'.Output (OUTPUT)
:P.Where the command sends what it produces&colon. to the display of an
interactive job, or to a spooled file of the job's printer file. Some
commands can also write it to a database file.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*:EPK.
:PD.The output is shown at the display of an interactive job, and
printed for a batch job.
:PT.:PK.*PRINT:EPK.
:PD.The output is printed with the job's spooled output.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKUSRPRF/ASTLVL'.Assistance level (ASTLVL)
:P.The assistance level the user's displays show&colon. basic
(Operational Assistant), intermediate (the system displays) or advanced.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*PRV:EPK.
:PD.The previous release.
:PT.:PK.*BASIC:EPK.
:PD.Basic.
:PT.:PK.*INTERMED:EPK.
:PD.Intermediate assistance&colon. the system displays.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
